# A to-do list you can keep on disk:
#   ./intent build examples/todo.intent -o build/todo
#   ./build/todo my.todo

Tasks is a collection.
Each task has an id (number), a title, a priority (number) and a done (number).
Ids are unique. Reject duplicates.
Keep tasks in the order they were added.

An open task is a task whose done is 0.
A finished task is a task whose done is 1.
"urgent" means with a priority of at least 3.

Add a task.
finish: set done to 1 for the task whose id is a given id.
reopen: set done to 0 for the task whose id is a given id.
bump: increase the priority by 1 for tasks whose id is a given id.
drop: remove a task by id.

todo: show the open tasks.
next: show the title of the open task with the highest priority.
urgent: show the titles of the urgent open tasks.
done: show the titles of the finished tasks.
How many open tasks are there?
tidy: remove the finished tasks.
